                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "20526cae-d4d9-451f-a927-cfcdf5c2b7e4",
                        "entry_id": "71344021-040d-3d37-a36a-ce6b279b5dde",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "jovialités"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1deed29a-1304-38a4-a079-38eb8e603373",
                        "entry_id": "71344021-040d-3d37-a36a-ce6b279b5dde",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Humeur joviale."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a289958c-9fb1-4aa6-8ceb-d24bb8fbad16",
                                "sense_id": "1deed29a-1304-38a4-a079-38eb8e603373",
                                "text": "Il est d’une jovialité fatigante."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cb056f5b-3f9c-40e4-8970-32552ef3ab67",
                                "sense_id": "1deed29a-1304-38a4-a079-38eb8e603373",
                                "text": "Les économistes sont fréquemment perçus comme d’affreux rabatjoie qui veulent noyer la jovialité naturelle et l’affection mutuelle des êtres humains dans une potion indigeste de rigueur économique."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "74d98ded-4826-4557-9034-e4f22a0e0bed",
                        "source_entry_id": "71344021-040d-3d37-a36a-ce6b279b5dde",
                        "source_sense_id": "1deed29a-1304-38a4-a079-38eb8e603373",
                        "target_lang_word": "joviality",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "joviality",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bde2c1b9-3afa-3d5d-9963-bd9e409f1660",
                                        "entry_id": "0207af54-a926-3baf-948d-e103dd40ff82",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state of being jovial; jollity or conviviality."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f71c510e-a143-4637-8c6f-8db492a17958",
                                                "sense_id": "bde2c1b9-3afa-3d5d-9963-bd9e409f1660",
                                                "text": "1651, Fulgenzio Micanzio, The Life of the Most Learned Father Paul, Of the Order of the Servie, translator not credited, London: Humphrey Moseley and Richard Marriot, p. 13,\nThe Duke […] willingly interposed the pleasures of wit and facetiousnesse with the grave cares of his government, tempering wisely his troubles with Joviality of words and actions […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9d6c3d2f-dce9-40a1-adfe-2c1ca0632d83",
                                                "sense_id": "bde2c1b9-3afa-3d5d-9963-bd9e409f1660",
                                                "text": "I noticed that Mr. Pumblechook in his hospitality appeared to forget that he had made a present of the wine, but took the bottle from Mrs. Joe and had all the credit of handing it about in a gush of joviality."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e58ac301-43f7-4366-afba-e85c8e44f2f3",
                                                "sense_id": "bde2c1b9-3afa-3d5d-9963-bd9e409f1660",
                                                "text": "This remark sobered the father’s joviality, and brought his mind to business."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4e22ec3f-32df-4c44-b0f4-e8818cc868f3",
                                                "sense_id": "bde2c1b9-3afa-3d5d-9963-bd9e409f1660",
                                                "text": "By the joviality of their insults Babbitt knew that he had been taken back to their hearts, and happily he rose."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "22741f51-2d5c-4fe4-8bf1-d896ca610270",
                                                "sense_id": "bde2c1b9-3afa-3d5d-9963-bd9e409f1660",
                                                "text": "Joviality fled from the table, Shekhar studied his cards. Owad frowned at his. His foot was tapping on the concrete floor. More watchers came."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8207da15-49d8-49bc-b5c7-def1519bdbfc",
                                                "sense_id": "bde2c1b9-3afa-3d5d-9963-bd9e409f1660",
                                                "text": "Success on social media tends to instil in the early career academics and postgraduates who achieve it, after merciless encouragement from outreach and impact gurus in HE management, a kind of unwavering, po-faced self-belief in their own genius and thus the vital urgency of their research, the overall effect being a strange mixture of corporate cynicism and uneasy joviality."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2099131d-547f-4b6a-9151-a190978426bb",
                        "source_entry_id": "71344021-040d-3d37-a36a-ce6b279b5dde",
